{"content_hash": "eab261c58bfe761c", "version_id": 568, "article_id": 57, "level_code": "ja_n3", "lang": "ja", "level": 3, "level_label": "N3 中級", "title": "ロシアの滑空爆弾がザポリージャを攻撃、子ども4人を含む20人以上が死亡", "title_zh": "俄罗斯滑翔炸弹袭击扎波罗热，至少20人死亡，其中包括4名儿童", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwvgdpv642g5o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1765180520768-aa3ef0ea7b37?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8M3x8cnVzc2lhbiUyMGdsaWRlJTIwYm9tYnxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNjc4MzEwfDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Alex Ko on Unsplash", "author": "Alex Ko", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@alexko?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/aeroflot-airplane-on-the-tarmac-at-an-airport-MPK9BSV2mok?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(169, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(207, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "ac39eda995dc"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-10", "word_count": 221, "reading_minutes": 0.7, "lead": "10月10日、ロシア軍がウクライナ南部のザポリージャを滑空爆弾で攻撃しました。地元の役人によると、子ども4人を含む少なくとも20人が死亡し、32人以上がけがをしました。", "lead_zh": "10月10日，俄军用滑翔炸弹袭击了乌克兰南部的扎波罗热。据当地官员说，至少20人死亡，其中包括4名儿童，另有32人以上受伤。", "preview": "攻撃は土曜日の朝、住宅の建物に当たりました。けがをした人は少なくとも32人いて、まだ行方不明の人も多く、がれきの下にいると思われます。あるアパートはほとんど壊れてしまいました。市の代行市長は「1階に爆弾が当たり、上の階がそのまま崩れた」と話しました。", "preview_zh": "袭击发生在周六早上，击中了居民楼。至少32人受伤，还有很多人失踪，据信被埋在瓦砾下。一栋公寓几乎被完全摧毁。代理市长说：“炸弹击中了一楼，上面的楼层直接塌了下来。”", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 556, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/57/ja_n3.mp3", "duration": 47.762, "size_bytes": 290304, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 160, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/568.json", "paragraphs": ["攻撃は土曜日の朝、住宅の建物に当たりました。けがをした人は少なくとも32人いて、まだ行方不明の人も多く、がれきの下にいると思われます。あるアパートはほとんど壊れてしまいました。市の代行市長は「1階に爆弾が当たり、上の階がそのまま崩れた」と話しました。", "80人以上の作業員が救助活動を続けています。救助隊は時々手を止めて、がれきの下にいる人の音を聞こうとします。代行市長は、ロシアは「私たちの心」を攻撃し、「一番小さな子どもたち」が亡くなったと話し、家族にとってとても悲しいことだと述べました。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["袭击发生在周六早上，击中了居民楼。至少32人受伤，还有很多人失踪，据信被埋在瓦砾下。一栋公寓几乎被完全摧毁。代理市长说：“炸弹击中了一楼，上面的楼层直接塌了下来。”", "80多名工作人员仍在继续救援。救援人员不时停下来，倾听瓦砾下幸存者发出的声音。代理市长说，俄罗斯袭击了“我们的心脏”，“最小的孩子们”遇难了，这对家人来说是极其悲痛的事。"], "body": "攻撃は土曜日の朝、住宅の建物に当たりました。けがをした人は少なくとも32人いて、まだ行方不明の人も多く、がれきの下にいると思われます。あるアパートはほとんど壊れてしまいました。市の代行市長は「1階に爆弾が当たり、上の階がそのまま崩れた」と話しました。\n\n80人以上の作業員が救助活動を続けています。救助隊は時々手を止めて、がれきの下にいる人の音を聞こうとします。代行市長は、ロシアは「私たちの心」を攻撃し、「一番小さな子どもたち」が亡くなったと話し、家族にとってとても悲しいことだと述べました。", "body_zh": "袭击发生在周六早上，击中了居民楼。至少32人受伤，还有很多人失踪，据信被埋在瓦砾下。一栋公寓几乎被完全摧毁。代理市长说：“炸弹击中了一楼，上面的楼层直接塌了下来。”\n\n80多名工作人员仍在继续救援。救援人员不时停下来，倾听瓦砾下幸存者发出的声音。代理市长说，俄罗斯袭击了“我们的心脏”，“最小的孩子们”遇难了，这对家人来说是极其悲痛的事。", "text": "攻撃は土曜日の朝、住宅の建物に当たりました。けがをした人は少なくとも32人いて、まだ行方不明の人も多く、がれきの下にいると思われます。あるアパートはほとんど壊れてしまいました。市の代行市長は「1階に爆弾が当たり、上の階がそのまま崩れた」と話しました。 80人以上の作業員が救助活動を続けています。救助隊は時々手を止めて、がれきの下にいる人の音を聞こうとします。代行市長は、ロシアは「私たちの心」を攻撃し、「一番小さな子どもたち」が亡くなったと話し、家族にとってとても悲しいことだと述べました。", "vocab": [{"word": "滑空爆弾", "pos": "noun", "zh": "滑翔炸弹", "note": "军事用语，指从飞机投放后滑翔飞行的炸弹", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "攻撃", "pos": "noun", "zh": "攻击、袭击", "note": "常用词，可作名词也可作动词する", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "死亡", "pos": "noun", "zh": "死亡", "note": "新闻中常用，比「死ぬ」更正式", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "けが", "pos": "noun", "zh": "受伤", "note": "日常词，也可说「けがをする」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "行方不明", "pos": "noun", "zh": "失踪、下落不明", "note": "常用于灾害或事故报道", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "がれき", "pos": "noun", "zh": "瓦砾、废墟", "note": "灾害新闻常见词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "救助", "pos": "noun", "zh": "救助、救援", "note": "常与「活動」「隊」搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "作業員", "pos": "noun", "zh": "工作人员、作业人员", "note": "指现场干活的人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "大統領", "pos": "noun", "zh": "总统", "note": "国家元首的称呼", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "制裁", "pos": "noun", "zh": "制裁", "note": "国际政治常用词，如「制裁を緩める」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "前線", "pos": "noun", "zh": "前线", "note": "战争语境中指交战地区", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "民間人", "pos": "noun", "zh": "平民、民间人士", "note": "与军人相对，新闻中常指非战斗人员", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Russian glide bomb attack on Zaporizhzhia kills at least 20 people", "summary_original": "Volodymyr Zelensky says the attack, which left children dead, was Russia expressing its \"thanks\" for a US diesel deal.", "body_original": "Russian glide bomb attack on Zaporizhzhia kills at least 20 people\nBy\nVitaly Shevchenko\nand\nTom McArthur\nPublished\n10 October 2026\nRussia has attacked the Ukrainian city of Zaporizhzhia with five glide bombs, killing at least 20 people including four children, local officials said.\nThe glide bombs hit residential buildings in the southern city on Saturday morning. At least\n32 others were injured in the attack, with more still missing and believed to be under the rubble.\nUkrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said the attacks on Zaporizhzhia were Russia expressing \"its thanks\" for a deal announced by US President Donald Trump last night easing sanctions on Moscow to import Russian diesel.\nHe added that 13 other regions had come under attack overnight, arguing this demonstrated Russia took \"any easing of pressure to mean they can keep fighting\".\nPhotos and videos from the site of one of the strikes in Zaporizhzhia show an apartment block mostly destroyed.\n\"The ground floor was hit, and the floors above just collapsed,\" acting Mayor Regina Harchenko told Ukrainian television from the scene.\nShe said more than 80 workers were involved in ongoing search and rescue operations which are expected to continue throughout the day.\nThe rescuers regularly stop to listen for any noises made by survivors who could be under the rubble.\nHarchenko said Russia had struck at \"our very heart\" and \"our littlest ones\" were among those killed, adding that their deaths were \"awful grief for their families. For the city.\"\nZaporizhzhia is a major regional centre with more than 700,000 residents. It is located less than 10 miles (16km) from the front line\nand is frequently attacked by Russian drones and missiles\n.\nTrump announces deal for Russian diesel as Zelensky calls it a gift to Putin\nPublished\n9 hours ago\nAnalysis: Trump's shock Russia deal highlights mounting pressure to curb fuel prices\nPublished\n1 day ago\nZelensky was quick to criticise Trump's diesel deal with Russia, calling it\na gift to Russian President Vladimir Putin\n. Analysts view the deal as an attempt by the US president to allay domestic concerns about high fuel prices ahead of the upcoming midterm elections.\nZelensky wrote on social media on Saturday that Russian attacks on energy facilities in the capital, Kyiv, demonstrated Russia's \"true intentions\".\n\"Russia's choice is war. And they will be ready to end it only when they feel that their ability to drag the war out is diminishing.\n\"Unfortunately, the signals Russia received yesterday were entirely different – signals suggesting that it could simply keep attacking. And this needs to be corrected.\"\nBoth Russia and Ukraine have stepped up attacks on infrastructure in recent months, as Moscow's full-scale invasion, launched in 2022, drags on.\nOn Thursday, at least 33 people were killed in another Russian glide bomb attack on two civilian buses in Kramatorsk, in the eastern Donetsk region.\nThe day before,\n22 people including five children\ndied as a Russian missile hit an apartment block in the town of Pryluky, east of Kyiv.\nThe number of civilian casualties in Ukraine\njumped by 55%\n,\nexternal\nin the first eight months of this year, according to the UN.\nRussia has\nalso stepped up its attacks on Ukrainian energy infrastructure\nas winter approaches, a strategy it has undertaken in previous years. Kyiv has repeatedly accused it of targeting Ukraine's civilian population, which Moscow denies.\nFor its part, Ukraine has increasingly adopted a policy of striking infrastructure often deep inside Russia that is crucial to its economy, including several oil refineries and terminals.\nSeveral\nstrikes on data centres owned by Yandex\nhave left the tech giant struggling to maintain services.\nKyiv says its strikes are aimed at curtailing revenue streams for Russia's war machine.\nRelated topics\nWar in Ukraine\nUkraine\nMore on this story\nWatch: Fleeing Kyiv for the countryside ahead of winter\nPublished\n1 day ago\nFear and disruption for Ukraine's rail passengers as Russia escalates drone attacks\nPublished\n4 days ago\nRussia targeting 'ordinary life' with attacks on Ukraine's data centres, Zelensky says\nPublished\n25 September", "fetched_at": "2026-10-11T00:25:09.061571", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "攻撃", "s": 0.163, "e": 0.6, "sm": 162, "em": 600, "cs": 0, "ce": 2, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "は", "s": 0.613, "e": 0.75, "sm": 612, "em": 750, "cs": 2, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "土曜日", "s": 0.762, "e": 1.262, "sm": 762, "em": 1262, "cs": 3, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "の", "s": 1.275, "e": 1.375, "sm": 1275, "em": 1375, "cs": 6, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "朝", "s": 1.387, "e": 1.788, "sm": 1387, "em": 1787, "cs": 7, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "、", "s": 1.788, "e": 2.075, "sm": 1787, "em": 2075, "cs": 8, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "住宅", "s": 2.075, "e": 2.538, "sm": 2075, "em": 2537, "cs": 9, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "の", "s": 2.55, "e": 2.662, "sm": 2550, "em": 2662, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "建物", "s": 2.675, "e": 3.15, "sm": 2675, "em": 3150, "cs": 12, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "に", "s": 3.163, "e": 3.288, "sm": 3162, "em": 3287, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "当たり", "s": 3.3, "e": 3.625, "sm": 3300, "em": 3625, "cs": 15, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "まし", "s": 3.638, "e": 3.863, "sm": 3637, "em": 3862, 